### Topic 56 - GraphQL sample requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
### Every request is a POST to the SAME url. Only the query text changes.
### Tip: GraphiQL in the browser is even nicer: http://localhost:8080/graphiql

@url = http://localhost:8080/graphql

### 1. All books - only title + author name (no over-fetching!)
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ books { title author { name } } }" }

### 2. One book by id
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ bookById(id: 1) { id title pages } }" }

### 3. An author and all their books (nested query, one round trip)
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ authorById(id: 2) { name country books { title pages } } }" }

### 4. Search books by title
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ searchBooks(title: \"head first\") { title } }" }

### 5. Mutation with VARIABLES (the recommended way)
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation AddBook($input: BookInput!) { addBook(input: $input) { id title author { name } } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "title": "Spring Boot Up and Running", "pages": 300, "authorId": 3 } }
}

### 6. Delete a book
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "mutation { deleteBook(id: 2) }" }

### 7. Error: delete a missing book -> "errors" array with NOT_FOUND (HTTP status is still 200)
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "mutation { deleteBook(id: 99) }" }

### 8. Error: asking for a field that does not exist -> ValidationError
POST {{url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ books { isbn } }" }

### 9. The schema as text
GET http://localhost:8080/graphql/schema
